<% content_for :title, "Spinner" %>
<div class="mb-8">
  <p class="mb-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-primary">Components</p>
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-3">Spinner</h1>
  <p class="text-muted-foreground">
    An inline SVG loading indicator. Renders <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">role="status"</code>
    with an accessible name — "Loading" by default, or your own text passed as the block.
  </p>
</div>

<%# Preview %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Preview</h2>
<div id="spinner-preview" class="rounded-lg border border-border bg-muted flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-8 p-12 mb-8">
  <%= render Ui::SpinnerComponent.new %>
  <%= render Ui::SpinnerComponent.new(class: "size-6 text-primary") %>
  <%= render(Ui::SpinnerComponent.new(class: "text-muted-foreground")) { "Saving changes" } %>
  <%= render(Ui::ButtonComponent.new(disabled: true, class: "gap-2")) do %>
    <%= render Ui::SpinnerComponent.new(class: "text-current", aria: { hidden: true }) %>
    Saving…
  <% end %>
</div>

<%# Usage %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Usage</h2>
<div class="rounded-lg overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800 mb-8">
  <div class="flex items-center justify-between bg-neutral-900 px-4 py-2">
    <span class="text-xs text-neutral-400">ERB</span>
    <button data-copy-target="#spinner-usage" class="text-xs text-neutral-400 hover:text-white transition-colors">Copy</button>
  </div>
  <pre class="bg-neutral-950 px-5 py-4 overflow-x-auto text-sm leading-relaxed" tabindex="0"><code id="spinner-usage" class="text-neutral-200"><%= h(example_spinner_usage) %></code></pre>
</div>

<%# Options %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Options</h2>
<div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border mb-8">
  <table class="w-full text-sm">
    <thead class="bg-muted">
      <tr>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Name</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Type</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Default</th>
        <th class="text-left px-4 py-3 text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground uppercase tracking-wider">Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-border">
      <% [
        ["block",  "String", '"Loading"', "The accessible name, read by a screen reader. Rendered visually hidden — it never shows on screen, so pass whatever text describes the wait."],
        ["class",  "String", "nil",       "Merged over the default classes with tailwind_merge — size the icon with [:where(&>svg)]:size-* or colour it with text-*."],
        ["…",      "Any",    "—",         "Every other keyword (id:, data:, aria:, …) is forwarded to the root element."],
      ].each do |name, type, default, desc| %>
        <tr class="hover:bg-muted/50">
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-primary"><%= name %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= type %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 font-mono text-xs text-muted-foreground"><%= default %></td>
          <td class="px-4 py-3 text-muted-foreground"><%= desc %></td>
        </tr>
      <% end %>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<%# Notes %>
<h2 class="text-base font-semibold mb-3">Notes</h2>
<ul class="space-y-2 text-sm text-neutral-600 dark:text-neutral-400 list-disc list-inside">
  <li><code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">role="status"</code> plus a visually hidden name announces the spinner once, the way a live region should — it doesn't renarrate on every animation frame.</li>
  <li>The svg itself is <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">aria-hidden="true"</code>; the accessible name comes only from the hidden text, so an icon-only spinner is never announced as blank.</li>
  <li>Colour comes from <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">currentColor</code>, so <code class="text-xs bg-neutral-100 dark:bg-neutral-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded">text-*</code> classes (or a parent's text colour, inside a disabled button) control it.</li>
  <li>No Stimulus controller. Show it conditionally from your own state — a Turbo Stream, a disabled button, a loading flag.</li>
</ul>
